WEBVTT

00:00:04.679 --> 00:00:07.830
<v Callum Reid>Morning, everyone. All eight of us on? Right, lovely.</v>

00:00:08.359 --> 00:00:13.259
<v Sarah Okafor>Before we start, there's a birthday cake in the office. Quite a substantial one.</v>

00:00:15.240 --> 00:00:16.640
<v David Whitfield>Whose birthday is it?</v>

00:00:18.789 --> 00:00:22.640
<v Sarah Okafor>Couldn't tell you. I got as far as seeing the cake.</v>

00:00:23.710 --> 00:00:24.910
<v Jamie Brennan>Excellent traceability there.</v>

00:00:25.539 --> 00:00:29.039
<v Hannah Price>Don't bring quality into it. I'm having a slice regardless.</v>

00:00:30.309 --> 00:00:34.509
<v Marcus Hale>Am I coming through? I've got you all sounding like you're underwater.</v>

00:00:34.850 --> 00:00:38.000
<v Olumide Adeyemi>You're clear our end. Is that your headset again?</v>

00:00:39.060 --> 00:00:41.159
<v Marcus Hale>Yeah, there we go. Better now.</v>

00:00:43.179 --> 00:00:45.630
<v Callum Reid>Right, quick round of the carry-overs first.</v>

00:00:46.640 --> 00:00:55.740
<v Jamie Brennan>Callum Reid asked me to pass this one on: the permit to work and isolation for the line 2 guard are now due on the 3rd.</v>

00:00:56.630 --> 00:00:57.829
<v Callum Reid>Cheers, yes.</v>

00:00:58.939 --> 00:01:06.290
<v Priya Raman>And stores Jamie asked me to say the lock-out tag-out sign-off on the little water valve on two is all done.</v>

00:01:08.709 --> 00:01:12.209
<v Jamie Brennan>Thanks, Priya. Had that written down somewhere under my keyboard.</v>

00:01:12.969 --> 00:01:16.469
<v Hannah Price>My filter swap on the tower is sorted. All done.</v>

00:01:17.670 --> 00:01:18.870
<v David Whitfield>Nice one.</v>

00:01:20.329 --> 00:01:25.579
<v Sarah Okafor>Yeah, and mine's sorted as well—the jam's cleared and I've checked the sensors. All finished.</v>

00:01:26.420 --> 00:01:27.620
<v Callum Reid>Lovely, thanks.</v>

00:01:28.250 --> 00:01:34.900
<v Callum Reid>I got over to Harbour Road and picked up the replacement parts for the stacker. That one's boxed off.</v>

00:01:36.859 --> 00:01:39.310
<v Jamie Brennan>Was the traffic as grim as usual?</v>

00:01:40.579 --> 00:01:44.780
<v Callum Reid>Oh, absolutely. Plenty of time to admire the same set of lights.</v>

00:01:47.260 --> 00:01:49.010
<v Marcus Hale>Scenic route. Without the scenery.</v>

00:01:50.250 --> 00:01:56.200
<v Callum Reid>Pretty much. Also, the function test on the heater box on one is finished, all signed off.</v>

00:01:57.150 --> 00:01:58.349
<v Priya Raman>Lovely.</v>

00:01:59.329 --> 00:02:05.280
<v Olumide Adeyemi>And just so you're aware, I already swapped the filter on the air compressor yesterday. That's done.</v>

00:02:07.510 --> 00:02:08.710
<v Callum Reid>Cheers.</v>

00:02:09.169 --> 00:02:19.319
<v Hannah Price>Only other thing from my walk through: saw the pressure on the barrel on three dip for a few minutes. It came back on its own. Just an observation.</v>

00:02:21.689 --> 00:02:24.490
<v David Whitfield>Sorry, I talked over the end of that.</v>

00:02:25.759 --> 00:02:28.210
<v Hannah Price>No, you're all right. That was all.</v>

00:02:28.680 --> 00:02:30.780
<v Callum Reid>Okay. New bits for today, then.</v>

00:02:31.590 --> 00:02:35.439
<v Callum Reid>Marcus Hale, can you inspect the feedwater pump for leaks, please?</v>

00:02:36.370 --> 00:02:39.169
<v Marcus Hale>Yeah, I'll inspect the feedwater pump for leaks.</v>

00:02:41.469 --> 00:02:42.669
<v Callum Reid>Ta.</v>

00:02:43.569 --> 00:02:48.819
<v Marcus Hale>Sorry, heard my name and Teams froze for a second. Got the actual request, though.</v>

00:02:50.449 --> 00:02:52.550
<v Olumide Adeyemi>It's picking its moments this morning.</v>

00:02:54.460 --> 00:02:55.860
<v Callum Reid>Always does. Guarding next—</v>

00:02:56.960 --> 00:03:02.560
<v Hannah Price>Yeah, I'll check the guarding on the Engel by 11am. That one's safety critical, straight away.</v>

00:03:03.020 --> 00:03:04.770
<v Sarah Okafor>Yes, absolutely. No argument there.</v>

00:03:05.240 --> 00:03:07.689
<v Callum Reid>Thanks. Hannah Price on the guarding, then.</v>

00:03:09.430 --> 00:03:10.629
<v Hannah Price>Yep.</v>

00:03:11.000 --> 00:03:13.099
<v David Whitfield>Sorry, was that eleven you said?</v>

00:03:15.300 --> 00:03:17.750
<v Hannah Price>By 11am, yeah. I'm starting straight away.</v>

00:03:19.919 --> 00:03:22.719
<v David Whitfield>Got you. Audio's a bit woolly this end.</v>

00:03:23.719 --> 00:03:26.520
<v Priya Raman>You're not the only one. Comes and goes.</v>

00:03:27.830 --> 00:03:29.030
<v Callum Reid>And stores?</v>

00:03:30.259 --> 00:03:34.460
<v Jamie Brennan>Yeah, I'll order spare parts for the BFP. Low priority, that one.</v>

00:03:34.800 --> 00:03:36.000
<v Callum Reid>Thanks, stores Jamie.</v>

00:03:37.960 --> 00:03:40.409
<v Jamie Brennan>That's me. Less glamorous than it sounds.</v>

00:03:41.069 --> 00:03:43.169
<v Marcus Hale>Depends how you feel about cardboard.</v>

00:03:44.240 --> 00:03:45.439
<v Jamie Brennan>Strong opinions, actually.</v>

00:03:46.870 --> 00:03:50.719
<v Callum Reid>Right, that's the lot from me. Anything else for this stand-up?</v>

00:03:52.500 --> 00:03:53.900
<v Priya Raman>Nothing else from me.</v>

00:03:54.509 --> 00:03:55.710
<v David Whitfield>No, all good.</v>

00:03:56.180 --> 00:04:00.729
<v Sarah Okafor>Only that the cake isn't going to survive eight people knowing about it.</v>

00:04:01.050 --> 00:04:04.550
<v Callum Reid>Well, now we know what everyone's thinking about. Cheers, everyone.</v>

00:04:06.960 --> 00:04:09.060
<v Marcus Hale>Cheers, see you in a bit.</v>
